t of which particulars had been concealed, the Hon’ble High Court has held that therefore the Tribunal was justified In invoking the provisions of Explanation as they stood on 10-2-1978, i.e., the date of filing the return, Shri Anadi Verma, learned Departmental Representative relied upon the decision of Tribunal, Calcutta Bench in the case of Asstt. CIT v. Mcleod Russel (I) Ltd. [2006] 101 ITD 39 (Kol.) in which it has been held that claiming of excess deduction also amounts to concealment of income, Shri Anadi Verma, learned senior Departmental Representative also relied on the following observations of the Tribunal, Pune Bench ‘B’ in the case of Proj. Industries Ltd. v. Jt. CIT [2009] 118 ITD 447 (Pune), the Pune Bench of the Tribunal has referred to its earlier decision in the case of Asstt. CIT v. Malhotra Mukesh Satpal [2008] 115 ITD 467 (Pune) wherein the Tribunal has concluded and summarized the scope and effect of section 271(1)(c) read with Explanation 1 as under :

